--
-- Tests for bc-interpretation-powers.l4 (Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238, ss 17, 19, 21, 22, 23, 27, 41).
-- Each expected value was decided from the text before the file was first run. Every limb of a rule is tested on both
-- sides. A case the text does not answer is asserted as the named refusal with its message (NOTES.md, finding 2).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-powers`


§ `s 17 Corporate rights and powers`
-- 17 (1): "A corporation has perpetual succession and may do the following:" (a) to (f).
#ASSERT `s 17(1) a corporation has perpetual succession`
#ASSERT `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` `Sue and be sued in its corporate name`
#ASSERT `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` `Contract and be contracted with in its corporate name`
#ASSERT `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` `Have a common seal, and alter or change it`
#ASSERT `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` `Regulate its own procedure and business`
-- (d) "acquire and dispose of property other than land for its purposes": both limbs.
#ASSERT `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` (`Acquire or dispose of property` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` (`Acquire or dispose of property` TRUE TRUE)
        BECAUSE "s 17(1) lists what a corporation may do and does not say it may do nothing else"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` (`Acquire or dispose of property` FALSE FALSE)
        BECAUSE "s 17(1) lists what a corporation may do and does not say it may do nothing else"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` (`Acquire or dispose of property` TRUE FALSE)
        BECAUSE "s 17(1) lists what a corporation may do and does not say it may do nothing else"
-- (f) the bilingual-name condition.
#ASSERT `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` (`Use either form of its name or both, and show both forms on its seal or have 2 seals` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` (`Use either form of its name or both, and show both forms on its seal or have 2 seals` FALSE)
        BECAUSE "s 17(1) lists what a corporation may do and does not say it may do nothing else"
-- "may do the following" lists what a corporation may do; the text does not say it may do nothing else (fork F-open-list).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` `Do something else`
        BECAUSE "s 17(1) lists what a corporation may do and does not say it may do nothing else"

-- 17 (2): "A majority of the members of the corporation may bind the others and the corporation by their acts." A majority is more than half.
#ASSERT `s 17(2) the members who act may bind the others and the corporation` 3 2
#ASSERT `s 17(2) the members who act may bind the others and the corporation` 4 3
#ASSERT `s 17(2) the members who act may bind the others and the corporation` 1 1
#ASSERT `s 17(2) the members who act may bind the others and the corporation` 5 5
-- Exactly half is not a majority, and the text does not say what fewer than a majority may do.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 17(2) the members who act may bind the others and the corporation` 4 2
        BECAUSE "s 17(2) says what a majority of the members may do and does not say what fewer may do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 17(2) the members who act may bind the others and the corporation` 3 1
        BECAUSE "s 17(2) says what a majority of the members may do and does not say what fewer may do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 17(2) the members who act may bind the others and the corporation` 0 0
        BECAUSE "s 17(2) says what a majority of the members may do and does not say what fewer may do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 17(2) the members who act may bind the others and the corporation` 3 4
        BECAUSE "s 17(2) is not given a number acting that is more than the number of members"

-- 17 (3): "Individual members of a corporation established by an enactment who do not contravene the enactment are exempt from personal liability"
#ASSERT `s 17(3) the member is exempt from personal liability for the corporation's debts, obligations or acts` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 17(3) the member is exempt from personal liability for the corporation's debts, obligations or acts` TRUE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 17(3) speaks only of a member who does not contravene the enactment that established the corporation"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 17(3) the member is exempt from personal liability for the corporation's debts, obligations or acts` FALSE FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 17(3) speaks only of a member who does not contravene the enactment that established the corporation"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 17(3) the member is exempt from personal liability for the corporation's debts, obligations or acts` FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 17(3) speaks only of a member who does not contravene the enactment that established the corporation"

§ `s 19 Powers to judges and court officers`
-- 19 (1): "judicial or quasi judicial powers are given to a judge or officer of a court, the judge or officer in exercising the powers does so in the judge's or officer's official capacity and representing the court."
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the holder exercises the power in the holder's official capacity and represents the court` `A judge of a court` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the holder exercises the power in the holder's official capacity and represents the court` `An officer of a court` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 19(1) the holder exercises the power in the holder's official capacity and represents the court` `Someone else` TRUE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 19(1) speaks only of judicial or quasi judicial powers given by an enactment to a judge or officer of a court"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 19(1) the holder exercises the power in the holder's official capacity and represents the court` `A judge of a court` FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 19(1) speaks only of judicial or quasi judicial powers given by an enactment to a judge or officer of a court"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 19(1) the holder exercises the power in the holder's official capacity and represents the court` `A judge of a court` TRUE FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 19(1) speaks only of judicial or quasi judicial powers given by an enactment to a judge or officer of a court"
-- 19 (2): "if under an enactment an appeal is given from a person, board, commission or other body to a court or judge, an appeal lies from the decision of the court or judge"
#ASSERT `s 19(2) an appeal lies from the decision of the court or judge as in any other proceeding in that court` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 19(2) an appeal lies from the decision of the court or judge as in any other proceeding in that court` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 19(2) speaks only of an appeal given under an enactment from a person, board, commission or other body to a court or judge"

§ `s 21 Demise of the Crown`
-- 21: "it is not necessary to renew a commission or appointment ... all persons who held or exercised an office or profession under the late Sovereign continue in the exercise of the duties and functions ... and it is not necessary for those persons to take an oath of allegiance to the new Sovereign."
#ASSERT NOT (`s 21 the commission or appointment must be renewed` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 21 the person continues in the duties and functions of the office or profession` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 21 the person must take an oath of allegiance to the new Sovereign` TRUE TRUE)
-- Without a demise of the Crown, or for a person who held no such office, the section says nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 21 the commission or appointment must be renewed` FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 21 speaks only of a person who held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign, on a demise of the Crown"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 21 the commission or appointment must be renewed` TRUE FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 21 speaks only of a person who held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign, on a demise of the Crown"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 21 the person continues in the duties and functions of the office or profession` FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 21 speaks only of a person who held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign, on a demise of the Crown"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 21 the person continues in the duties and functions of the office or profession` TRUE FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 21 speaks only of a person who held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign, on a demise of the Crown"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 21 the person must take an oath of allegiance to the new Sovereign` FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 21 speaks only of a person who held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign, on a demise of the Crown"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 21 the person must take an oath of allegiance to the new Sovereign` TRUE FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 21 speaks only of a person who held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign, on a demise of the Crown"

§ `s 22 Included powers`
-- 22: "Words in an enactment authorizing the appointment of a public officer include power to do the following:" (a) to (f).
#ASSERT `s 22 words authorizing the appointment of a public officer include the power` `Set the public officer's term of office` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22 words authorizing the appointment of a public officer include the power` `Terminate the public officer's appointment, or remove or suspend the public officer` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22 words authorizing the appointment of a public officer include the power` `Reappoint or reinstate the public officer` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22 words authorizing the appointment of a public officer include the power` `Set the public officer's remuneration, and vary or terminate it` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22 words authorizing the appointment of a public officer include the power` `Appoint another in the public officer's place or to act in the public officer's place` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22 words authorizing the appointment of a public officer include the power` `Appoint a person as the public officer's deputy` TRUE
-- "include" leaves the list open (fork F-open-list).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 22 words authorizing the appointment of a public officer include the power` `Another power over the public officer` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 22 lists the powers such words include and does not say they include no others"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 22 words authorizing the appointment of a public officer include the power` `Set the public officer's term of office` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 22 speaks only of words in an enactment authorizing the appointment of a public officer"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 22 words authorizing the appointment of a public officer include the power` `Another power over the public officer` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 22 speaks only of words in an enactment authorizing the appointment of a public officer"

§ `s 23 Powers to act for ministers, deputy ministers and public officers`
-- 23 (1): words directing or empowering a minister include a designated minister and the deputy or associate deputy. 23 (5): not a regulation as defined in the Regulations Act.
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the words naming a minister include` `A minister designated to act in the office` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the words naming a minister include` `The deputy of the minister` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the words naming a minister include` `The associate deputy of the minister` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(1) the words naming a minister include` `The deputy of the minister` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(1) the words naming a minister include` `The associate deputy of the minister` TRUE)
-- 23 (5) names a deputy and an associate deputy; a minister designated to act is not named.
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the words naming a minister include` `A minister designated to act in the office` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 23(1) the words naming a minister include` `Someone else` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 23(1) lists whom words naming a minister include and does not say they include no one else"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 23(1) the words naming a minister include` `Someone else` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 23(1) lists whom words naming a minister include and does not say they include no one else"
-- 23 (2): "an assistant deputy minister, or some other official authorized by the minister, has the powers and must perform the duties of the deputy minister."
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the official has the powers and must perform the duties of the deputy minister` (`An assistant deputy minister` TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the official has the powers and must perform the duties of the deputy minister` `Some other official authorized by the minister` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 23(2) the official has the powers and must perform the duties of the deputy minister` `Some other official not authorized by the minister` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 23(2) names an assistant deputy minister or an official authorized by the minister and no one else"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 23(2) the official has the powers and must perform the duties of the deputy minister` (`An assistant deputy minister` TRUE) FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 23(2) speaks only of a deputy minister who is absent or unable to act"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 23(2) the official has the powers and must perform the duties of the deputy minister` `Some other official authorized by the minister` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 23(2) speaks only of a deputy minister who is absent or unable to act"
-- Fork F-adm, first reading (the one this encoding takes): "authorized by the minister" qualifies "some other official" only.
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the official has the powers and must perform the duties of the deputy minister` (`An assistant deputy minister` FALSE) TRUE
-- 23 (3): words directing or empowering a public officer include a person acting for the officer or appointed to act in the office, and the deputy.
#ASSERT `s 23(3) the words naming a public officer include` `A person acting for the public officer`
#ASSERT `s 23(3) the words naming a public officer include` `A person appointed to act in the office`
#ASSERT `s 23(3) the words naming a public officer include` `The deputy of the public officer`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 23(3) the words naming a public officer include` `Someone else`
        BECAUSE "s 23(3) lists whom words naming a public officer include and does not say they include no one else"
-- 23 (4): "This section applies whether or not the office of a minister or public officer is vacant."
#ASSERT `s 23(4) section 23 applies` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(4) section 23 applies` FALSE

§ `s 27 Ancillary powers`
-- 27 (1): the thing "must be done by or before one whose jurisdiction or powers extend to the place where the thing is to be done."
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the thing may be done by or before the official` `A judge` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the thing may be done by or before the official` `A justice` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the thing may be done by or before the official` `A coroner` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the thing may be done by or before the official` `A public officer` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27(1) the thing may be done by or before the official` `A judge` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27(1) the thing may be done by or before the official` `A public officer` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27(1) the thing may be done by or before the official` `Another kind of person` TRUE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 27(1) speaks only of a thing that an enactment requires or authorizes to be done by or before a judge, justice, coroner or public officer"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27(1) the thing may be done by or before the official` `A judge` FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 27(1) speaks only of a thing that an enactment requires or authorizes to be done by or before a judge, justice, coroner or public officer"
-- 27 (2): "all the powers that are necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the doing of the act or thing are also deemed to be given."
#ASSERT `s 27(2) the power is deemed to be given` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27(2) the power is deemed to be given` TRUE FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 27(2) speaks only of the powers necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the doing of the act or thing"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27(2) the power is deemed to be given` FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 27(2) speaks only of the powers necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the doing of the act or thing"
-- 27 (3): "the power may be exercised and the duty must be performed from time to time as occasion requires."
#ASSERT `s 27(3) when a power may be exercised or a duty must be performed` `A power` EQUALS `The power may be exercised from time to time as occasion requires`
#ASSERT `s 27(3) when a power may be exercised or a duty must be performed` `A duty` EQUALS `The duty must be performed from time to time as occasion requires`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27(3) when a power may be exercised or a duty must be performed` `Something else`
        BECAUSE "s 27(3) speaks only of a power conferred or a duty imposed"
-- 27 (4): a power to make regulations "includes a power exercisable in the same manner, and subject to the same consent and conditions, if any, to repeal or amend the regulations and make others."
#ASSERT `s 27(4) a power to make regulations includes the power` `Repeal the regulations` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(4) a power to make regulations includes the power` `Amend the regulations` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(4) a power to make regulations includes the power` `Make other regulations` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27(4) a power to make regulations includes the power` `Something else` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 27(4) lists what a power to make regulations includes and does not say it includes nothing else"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27(4) a power to make regulations includes the power` `Amend the regulations` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 27(4) speaks only of an enactment that confers a power to make regulations"
#ASSERT `s 27(4) how the included power to repeal, amend or make others is exercised` (`How a power is exercised` WITH `the manner` IS "by order of the Lieutenant Governor in Council", `the consent and conditions, if any` IS (LIST "on the recommendation of the Minister")) EQUALS `How a power is exercised` WITH `the manner` IS "by order of the Lieutenant Governor in Council", `the consent and conditions, if any` IS (LIST "on the recommendation of the Minister")
-- 27 (5): "the Lieutenant Governor in Council or public officer has the power to do that other act or thing."
#ASSERT `s 27(5) the one who must do the other act has the power to do it` `The Lieutenant Governor in Council` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(5) the one who must do the other act has the power to do it` `A public officer` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27(5) the one who must do the other act has the power to do it` `Someone else` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 27(5) speaks only of an act of the Lieutenant Governor in Council or of a public officer on which an authorized act depends"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27(5) the one who must do the other act has the power to do it` `A public officer` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 27(5) speaks only of an act of the Lieutenant Governor in Council or of a public officer on which an authorized act depends"
-- 27 (6): the power to enter into an agreement includes the power of the other party to enter into it and carry out its terms, "subject to conditions that apply to that person".
#ASSERT `s 27(6) the person may enter into the agreement and carry out its terms` `The person with whom the agreement is to be made` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27(6) the person may enter into the agreement and carry out its terms` `The person with whom the agreement is to be made` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 27(6) the person may enter into the agreement and carry out its terms` `The person given the power` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27(6) the person may enter into the agreement and carry out its terms` `The person given the power` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27(6) the person may enter into the agreement and carry out its terms` `Someone else` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 27(6) speaks only of the person given the power to enter into an agreement and the person with whom it is to be made"
-- 27 (7): "the power includes the power to make copies or extracts of the records."
#ASSERT `s 27(7) the power to inspect or require the production of records includes the power` `Make copies of the records` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(7) the power to inspect or require the production of records includes the power` `Make extracts of the records` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27(7) the power to inspect or require the production of records includes the power` `Something else` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 27(7) lists what such a power includes and does not say it includes nothing else"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27(7) the power to inspect or require the production of records includes the power` `Make copies of the records` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 27(7) speaks only of a power to inspect or to require the production of records"

§ `s 41 Powers to make regulations`
-- 41 (1)(a): regulations "considered necessary and advisable, are ancillary to it, and are not inconsistent with it".
#ASSERT `s 41(1) the power to make regulations is construed as empowering` (`Make regulations considered necessary and advisable, ancillary to the enactment and not inconsistent with it` TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(1) the power to make regulations is construed as empowering` (`Make regulations considered necessary and advisable, ancillary to the enactment and not inconsistent with it` TRUE TRUE FALSE) TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 41(1)(a) speaks only of regulations that are considered necessary and advisable, ancillary to the enactment and not inconsistent with it"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(1) the power to make regulations is construed as empowering` (`Make regulations considered necessary and advisable, ancillary to the enactment and not inconsistent with it` FALSE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 41(1)(a) speaks only of regulations that are considered necessary and advisable, ancillary to the enactment and not inconsistent with it"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(1) the power to make regulations is construed as empowering` (`Make regulations considered necessary and advisable, ancillary to the enactment and not inconsistent with it` TRUE FALSE TRUE) TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 41(1)(a) speaks only of regulations that are considered necessary and advisable, ancillary to the enactment and not inconsistent with it"
-- (b) to (d)
#ASSERT `s 41(1) the power to make regulations is construed as empowering` `Provide for administrative and procedural matters for which no express, or only partial, provision has been made` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(1) the power to make regulations is construed as empowering` `Limit the application of a regulation in time or place or both` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(1) the power to make regulations is construed as empowering` `Prescribe the amount of a fee authorized by the enactment` TRUE
-- (e) "for a regulation made by or with the approval of the Lieutenant Governor in Council, that its contravention constitutes an offence"
#ASSERT `s 41(1) the power to make regulations is construed as empowering` (`Provide that contravention of a regulation is an offence` TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(1) the power to make regulations is construed as empowering` (`Provide that contravention of a regulation is an offence` FALSE) TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 41(1)(e) speaks only of a regulation made by or with the approval of the Lieutenant Governor in Council"
-- (f) "a penalty not greater than the penalties provided in the Offence Act": at the ceiling, below it, above it.
#ASSERT `s 41(1) the power to make regulations is construed as empowering` (`Provide that a person guilty of an offence under paragraph (e) is liable to a penalty` 100 200) TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(1) the power to make regulations is construed as empowering` (`Provide that a person guilty of an offence under paragraph (e) is liable to a penalty` 200 200) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 41(1) the power to make regulations is construed as empowering` (`Provide that a person guilty of an offence under paragraph (e) is liable to a penalty` 201 200) TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(1) the power to make regulations is construed as empowering` `Something else` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 41(1) lists what a power to make regulations is construed as empowering and does not say it empowers nothing else"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(1) the power to make regulations is construed as empowering` `Prescribe the amount of a fee authorized by the enactment` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 41(1) speaks only of an enactment that provides that the Lieutenant Governor in Council or any other person may make regulations"
-- 41 (2): "A regulation made under the authority of an enactment has the force of law."
#ASSERT `s 41(2) the regulation has the force of law` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(2) the regulation has the force of law` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 41(2) speaks only of a regulation made under the authority of an enactment"

